# {{ product_name_display }} — API

FastAPI service for {{ product_name_display }}.

## Getting started

```sh
just dev-setup       # nix shell + uv sync + pre-commit + .env skeleton
nix develop          # or `direnv allow` for automatic activation
just serve           # http://localhost:8000/docs
```

## Layout

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
├── app.py        # app factory + lifespan (open/close shared resources here)
├── config.py     # pydantic-settings; all config via {{ package_name | upper }}__* env vars
├── schemas.py    # pydantic request/response models — validate at the edge
└── routers/      # thin route handlers, one module per resource
tests/            # httpx TestClient tests; run in-process, no server needed
```

The `items` router is a working example backed by an in-memory dict. Swap the
store for your real backend and keep the shape: routers thin, validation in
schemas, storage behind a small interface.

## Commands

```sh
just lint          # ruff check + format check
just type-check    # mypy --strict
just test          # pytest with coverage
just ci            # all of the above — same as CI
just docker-run    # build and run the production image locally
```

## Configuration

All settings come from the environment with the `{{ package_name | upper }}__`
prefix (see `config.py`). `.env` is local-only and gitignored;
`just create-env-file` writes a documented skeleton.
